nodes.body:
@gau-nernst Rebased onto `3ddc6702` and reran FP8 TP2 on two L20s with the full source tree ([results and reproduction](https://github.com/positive666/vllm/tree/db8bbea532270205d8beb992d4c2900dd0dee10f/sm89-full-main-fp8-20261019)).

Across A/B/B/A, throughput changed **+0.29% / +0.30% / −0.03%** at C1/C2/C8; TPOT p50 changed **−0.29% / −0.33% / +2.01%**. All 576 requests succeeded. The benefit is small; this does not demonstrate a material general serving speedup.

20 reference tests and 78 bit-exact wrapper cases passed, including six 128-step graph checks. Profiles confirm the intended BV dispatch. Each start scored 16/16 on the arithmetic smoke screen; model texts vary even between identical-baseline restarts, so I am not claiming model-level bit-exactness.

